.TH ORO-PROCESS 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:process \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:process'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Example usage: import process from 'oro:process'
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBProcessEnvironmentEvent (extends Event)\fR
Event emitted by `env` when an environment variable is set, deleted, or otherwise changed.
.TP
\fBconstructor(type, key, value)\fR
Documented method exposed by this module.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fItype\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIkey\fR (string \\| symbol; required)
.br
\fIvalue\fR (ProcessEnvironmentValue; optional)
.TP
\fBProcessEnvironment (extends EventTarget)\fR
Observable environment store backing `process.env`.
.br
Listen on this object to receive `set`, `delete`, and `change` events while reading environment values through `process.env` or `env.proxy`.
.TP
\fBenv\fR
Emitted when an environment variable is set. Emitted when an environment variable is deleted. Emitted when an environment variable is changed (set or delete). Observable process\-environment state.
.br
`process.env` returns `env.proxy`, which behaves like a mutable object of string keys to string values. The exported `env` object itself is the `EventTarget` you can subscribe to for environment change events.
.TP
\fBversions()\fR
Reports the frozen legacy `process.versions.socket` identifier plus current Oro Runtime and native library versions.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIProcessVersionsMap\fR
.TP
\fBnextTick(callback, ...args)\fR
Adds callback to the 'nextTick' queue.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIcallback\fR (Function; required)
.TP
\fBhrtime(time)\fR
Computed high resolution time as a `BigInt`.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fItime\fR (Array<number>?; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIbigint\fR
.TP
\fBexit(code)\fR
Documented function exposed by this module.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIcode\fR (number; optional; default 0) The exit code. Default: 0.
.TP
\fBmemoryUsage()\fR
Returns an object describing the memory usage of the Node.js process measured in bytes.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIObject\fR
